wc - count lines, words and bytes on standard input

usage: wc [-l] [-w] [-c] [-]

  -l, --lines   print the number of lines (newline bytes)
  -w, --words   print the number of words (runs of non-white-space bytes)
  -c, --bytes   print the number of bytes
  -h, --help    print this text and exit
  -             read standard input (the default; the only input there is)

With no -l, -w or -c all three are printed, in that order.
Exit status: 0 success, 1 the request cannot be carried out, 2 bad usage.

